Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: recognise the Gemini PDA's SENINF/CAMSV pipeline

libcamera's simple pipeline handler matches on the media device's driver
name, from a table compiled into simple.cpp -- there is no configuration
file, so a device it does not know about is invisible no matter how
conformant it is.

The third field is swIspEnabled. It must be true here: CAMSV is a bypass
DMA that does not scale, crop or debayer, and there is no hardware
converter anywhere on this path, so the CPU software ISP is the only
thing that can turn packed RAW10 into something an ordinary application
will accept. With it false the camera enumerates and offers only
SGRBG10_CSI2P; with it true the same camera offers ABGR8888 from
160x120 up to 2584x1944.

Applies to libcamera v0.4.0 (35ed4b9), which is what Debian trixie ships
as 0.4.0-7.

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -201,6 +201,13 @@
 static const SimplePipelineInfo supportedDevices[] = {
 	{ "dcmipp", {}, false },
+	/*
+	 * Planet Gemini PDA (MT6797). SENINF CSI-2 receiver feeding the CAMSV
+	 * bypass DMA: sensor subdev -> gemini-seninf -> a video node carrying
+	 * packed RAW10. No converter of any kind on this path -- CAMSV does not
+	 * scale, crop or debayer -- so the software ISP does all of it.
+	 */
+	{ "gemini-camsv", {}, true },
 	{ "imx7-csi", { { "pxp", 1 } }, false },
 	{ "intel-ipu6", {}, true },
 	{ "j721e-csi2rx", {}, true },
